<title>UK: SOCCER-REGIS TOLD TO QUIT.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-REGIS TOLD TO QUIT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cyrille Regis, who won five England caps as a striker, has been advised by a specialist to retire at 38.</p>
<p>Regis, born in French Guyana, appeared for West Brom, Coventry, Aston Villa, Wolves and Wycombe Wanderers before joining Third Division Chester last season.</p>
<p>He played his last game in February, when a trapped nerve in a calf required an operation.</p>
